{"id":"chatcmpl-d11dbe7f-b590-4564-bc4d-9cc830ce952d","object":"chat.completion","created":1795247852,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a verification-first approach to medical image interpretation: rather than trusting a single expert tool's output, the agent cross-validated the finding using multiple independent tools (grounded report, phrase grounding) before committing to an answer. The pattern generalizes to any binary visual-diagnosis task where a single tool call could be unreliable, and where spatial localization can serve as corroborating evidence.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a task requires choosing between two spatially-opposite findings (left vs. right, upper vs. lower), first query an expert tool for a comparative judgment, then independently verify with a localization/grounding tool before answering.\",\n    \"Treat any single tool output as a hypothesis, not a conclusion: chain a second, methodologically-different tool to confirm before finalizing, especially for high-stakes or ambiguous visual judgments.\",\n    \"Use phrase grounding on the candidate finding's exact wording to check that the described abnormality localizes to the anatomically expected region, converting a verbal claim into spatial evidence.\",\n    \"When options are mutually exclusive and symmetric (A vs. B mirror each other), the decision reduces to a single comparative question; frame the expert query as a direct comparison to avoid ambiguous outputs.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Visual medical diagnosis (binary/symmetric options)\": \"Ask an expert tool a comparative question (which side/region is abnormal), then corroborate with a grounded report and phrase-grounding on the leading candidate before answering.\",\n    \"Any tool-assisted multiple-choice with two plausible options\": \"Use one tool to form a hypothesis and a second, independent tool to falsify/confirm it; only answer when both agree.\",\n    \"Spatial/localization tasks\": \"Convert the candidate answer into a phrase and ground it; verify the returned coordinates match the anatomically expected location.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the leading finding is supported by at least two independent tool outputs (expert judgment + localization/grounding) before selecting an option.\",\n    \"Verify the grounded location matches the expected anatomy for the chosen option (e.g., right-sided finding localizes to the right side of the image).\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":494,"total_tokens":952,"completion_tokens":458,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":494},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":458}}}